#: ../pwntools/docs/source/memleak.rst:6
msgid ":mod:`pwnlib.memleak` --- Helper class for leaking memory"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak:1
msgid "MemLeak is a caching and heuristic tool for exploiting memory leaks."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak:3
msgid "It can be used as a decorator, around functions of the form:"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak:5
msgid "def some_leaker(addr):"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak:6
msgid "... return data_as_string_or_None"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak:9
msgid ""
"It will cache leaked memory (which requires either non-randomized static "
"data or a continouous session). If required, dynamic or known data can be"
" set with the set-functions, but this is usually not required. If a byte "
"cannot be recovered, it will try to leak nearby bytes in the hope that "
"the byte is recovered as a side-effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../pwntools/docs/source/memleak.rst
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak:15
msgid "The leaker function."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak:17
msgid "How many bytes to search backwards in case an address does not work."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak:19
msgid ""
"Whether to reraise call :func:`pwnlib.log.warning` in case the leaker "
"function throws an exception."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak:21
msgid ""
"If set, persist the leak cache to this path and reload it on "
"construction, so leaked bytes are reused across runs."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak:24
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak.NoNewlines:1
msgid ""
"Wrapper for leak functions such that addresses which contain newline "
"bytes are not leaked."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak.NoNewlines:4
msgid ""
"This is useful if the address which is used for the leak is provided by "
"e.g. ``fgets()``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak.NoNulls:1
msgid ""
"Wrapper for leak functions such that addresses which contain NULL bytes "
"are not leaked."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak.NoNulls:4
#, python-format
msgid ""
"This is useful if the address which is used for the leak is read in via a"
" string-reading function like ``scanf(\"%s\")`` or smilar."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak.NoWhitespace:1
msgid ""
"Wrapper for leak functions such that addresses which contain whitespace "
"bytes are not leaked."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak.NoWhitespace:4
msgid ""
"This is useful if the address which is used for the leak is read in via "
"e.g. ``scanf()``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak.String:1
msgid ""
"Wrapper for leak functions which leak strings, such that a NULL "
"terminator is automaticall added."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.memleak.MemLeak.String:4
msgid ""
"This is useful if the data leaked is printed out as a NULL-terminated "
"string, via e.g. ``printf()``."
msgstr ""

